This file contains a list of the known bugs in the dltools package.

* dlplay: the -a, --firstframe option is parsed and range checked but its value
is never used, so the option silently has no effect and playback always starts
at the first frame in the input

* dlplay: 3:2 pulldown is not handled, so film content in a 59.94 field per
second transport stream plays with every other frame reported late. The coded
frames arrive at 23.976fps and each is displayed for either two or three fields,
which the stream signals with repeat_first_field, but every frame is scheduled
for one frame period of the display mode. Such a stream also plays out as
1080p29.97 rather than 1080i59.94, because ffmpeg reports the coded frames as
progressive. Reproduced with gladiator.1080i60.ts

* dlplay: the -p, --video-pid and -o, --audio-pid options are parsed into the
same variables which find_pid_for_stream_type() then overwrites, so for a
transport stream the pids given on the command line are ignored and the first
program is always played
